  "query_preview": "from near Richardton to Hettinger. SPC mesoanalysis \nshows these storms to be in an environment with 1000-1500 J/kg \nCAPE and 30 kts of effective bulk shear. But they are also now \nmoving into an area of increased CIN, and mid level lapse rates \nare mostly anchored to the moist adiabatic lapse rate. It \ntherefore seems unlikely that the intensity of convection will \nincrease beyond what has already been observed. Forecast \nadjustments for this update were driven by current observations \nand trends, but no major changes were made. Showers and \nthunderstorms should diminish from west to east through tonight.\nDid add a patchy fog mention to western parts of the state \ntonight into Saturday morning. This would mainly impact higher \nterrain areas where clouds could lower to the surface.",
